# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

Each time the API's rate limit refuses a request, in either of its two places in `run_route`, the server counts that refusal against the limiter's key (R157's `account:<profile id>` or `address:<ip hash>`). Those refusals are kept in a capped, swept window inside `RateLimiterState`. When a key's window holds more than `API_REJECTION_ALERT_THRESHOLD` refusals inside `API_REJECTION_ALERT_WINDOW_MS`, the server raises exactly one `log_alert("api.rejections.unusual", {key, rejected, windowMs})`. It raises it again only once a whole window has passed since that key's last alert. A key at or under the threshold raises nothing, and so do refusals spread past the window. The decisions the spec leaves open go in the new ruling R1717000.

